EXT. TANDEM BICYCLE RENTAL KIOSK - BOARDWALK - DAY

Salt air. A row of bright tandems chained to a rack. Five people in the sun.

WILHELMINA "BILLIE" ODUYA, 28, in a sundress, grips a handlebar. BEHIND her, THEO RASMUSSEN-KHAN, 30, fumbles with a helmet. Next to them, GRANDMA CORAZON ESPINOSA, 80, in a straw hat, adjusts her bifocals. Her grandson, JUAN-PABLO, 14, scowls at his phone. And the KIOSK OWNER, FRIDA LINDGREN, 50s, leans on the counter with a stopwatch.

She clicks it.

FRIDA
Start.

Theo mounts. Billie pushes off. The tandem wobbles. He steers right. She leans left. They crash into the rack.

He laughs. She stares daggers. He helps her up. She brushes off his hands.

Corazon watches. Nods approval. Juan-Pablo looks up from his phone, shrugs, and pockets it.

JUAN-PABLO
Abuela, don't.

CORAZON
Watch me.

She climbs on. Pats the seat behind her. He sighs, climbs on. They pedal off, smooth as silk, past the kiosk, past the pier, into the sun.

Frida clicks the stopwatch. Billie and Theo watch them go. Their hands find each other.
